+## Required external inference deployment
+
+An operator may set `BB_ACCOUNT_POOL_EXTERNAL_REQUIRED=1`,
+`BB_ACCOUNT_POOL_EXTERNAL_URL` (an HTTPS Tailnet origin without a path), and
+`BB_ACCOUNT_POOL_EXTERNAL_TOKEN` in the BB server environment. This selects an
+inference-only relay: both BB providers always use the authenticated BB hub,
+which replaces its machine credential with the external Bearer key. Missing or
+invalid route configuration fails launches as unavailable. Route failures never
+select local accounts. Thread bypass and ordinary pool settings do not override
+this deployment policy. Personal terminal client settings are unchanged.
+
+This mode registers no account login, inspection, refresh, usage worker or local
+pool management handlers. Administer the shared provider pool through its
+separate node management service. It relays Messages, token counting, Responses, Responses compact and model listing only; upstream admission may
+keep compact closed. Management and other routes remain absent. Native
+session headers are retained, redirects rejected and failed requests not replayed.
+Server environment changes require the normal explicit service reload; dynamic
+node changes belong to the external router. Existing running provider sessions
+must be drained and relaunched before claiming this policy covers them.
+
+Set the required marker on managed BB execution-daemon processes too, without
+copying the external key to workers. Local subscription usage/probes are then
+disabled. For model discovery, the BB server queries the router with its own
+private key and sends validated model facts through authenticated host commands;
+workers never receive that key or launch an unrouted catalogue probe. Missing
+router configuration or unavailable catalogue data fails catalogue refresh with
+no native fallback. The host-daemon protocol must be version 231 or newer.
+
+The required relay contract readiness marker is
+`REQUIRED_EXTERNAL_POOL_CONTRACT_VERSION = 1`. Disabling this server profile
+requires removing its required marker, not setting it to zero. Provisioning and
+service mapping remain owned by rosetta-machine apply/check/verify.
